    "title": "Pros and cons list",
    "body": "\nMicrosoft pros\n- [ ] More relevant to what I\u2019m doing now\n- [ ] Can meet more interns and researchers, more of a social life in Redmond\n- [ ] I can build systems even tho my mentors usually do empirical study \n- [ ] Very hot field right now, it\u2019s kinda relevant to all fields \n- [ ] Is it a better name than Adobe for agents \n\nMicrosoft cons\n- [x] Submitting to diff conferences like IEEE\n- [ ] Mentors are not as big name in HCI but bigger name in SWE research\n- [ ] Mentors excel at empirical research \n- [ ] Got it myself, so I could get it again if I wanted to bc it seems to be easier for me to get SWE research interviews \n- [ ] Do I wanna be pigeonholed into this field? I am ok w it rn bc it\u2019s helpful for my career \n\nAdobe pros \n- [ ] Mira is a huge name in HCI field\n- [ ] Get paid 3k more I think \n- [ ] I\u2019ve always wanted to try out creativity and video \n- [ ] Got it via Lydia connection so idk if I can get this particular internship  again \n- [ ] If I renege it\u2019s bad \n\nAdobe cons\n- [ ] In Boston there r only 5 intern, could be lonely\n- [ ] Valentina seems super quiet, would I go crazy?\n- [ ] Adobe isn\u2019t as big of a name in agents \n",
